The probability that at least two of the five dice show the same number is  

\[
1-\frac{\text{ways all dice are different}}{6^5}
=1-\frac{6\cdot5\cdot4\cdot3\cdot2}{6^5}
=1-\frac{720}{7776}
=\frac{7056}{7776}
=\frac{49}{54}.
\]

Thus the correct answer is **(B)**.

